==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# Art consisting of [[found object]]s.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=John Robert Colombo|title=All the poems of John Robert Colombo|volume=3|page=691
|passage=The fundamental principle of '''found art''' is the fact that the source of the esthetic impulse is found not in the ''objet d'art'' but in the eye of the beholder of the ''objet d'art''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=Leeana Tankersley|title=Found Art: Discovering Beauty in Foreign Places|page=13
|passage='''Found art''' is created when odd, disparate, unlikely, even long-abandoned castoffs are put together with other similarly unexpected remnants to create something new and, if all goes as planned, lovely.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=Steve Mynard|title=Learning through Adventurous Activities|page=108
|passage='''Found art''' is made out of natural (or sometimes unnatural) things that you find when out and about exploring. If you want some examples look at the sculptures of Andy Goldsworthy {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2016|author=Robert Craig Bunch|title=The Art of Found Objects: Interviews with Texas Artists|page=76
|passage=Rick Lowe of Project Row Houses [in Houston] has evolved from a young, hard-working artist whose '''found art''' is cultural preservation.}}

